# Written into checkouts by a tool outside this repo -- an `AGENTS.md` mirror of the
# root `CLAUDE.md`, produced by running it through `CLAUDE.md`->`AGENTS.md` and a
# case-insensitive `claude`->`Codex`. Nothing here generates it and nothing would
# regenerate it: Codex reads `CLAUDE.md` through `project_doc_fallback_filenames`, so a
# repo-level `AGENTS.md` is a second instruction tree that drifts from the first and is
# the copy nothing tests. devkit deleted its own tracked one in v0.6.0 and it came back
# twice through `git add -A` in sweep commits, because an untracked file no `.gitignore`
# excludes is invisible to every gate. Ignored rather than merely deleted for that
# reason, and pinned at the root so a genuine `AGENTS.md` inside a vendor directory is
# left alone.
/AGENTS.md

# Worktrees Claude Code cuts for itself under `--spawn worktree` / `--worktree`. This is
# NOT the `<workspace>/.worktrees/` box tier — that one lives outside every checkout and
# `worktree.py` owns it. These land *inside* the repo, so without this line every
# `git status` carries a nested checkout as untracked, `git add -A` stages the whole of
# it, and anything reading dirtiness (`sweep.classify`, the session-start banner) calls
# the checkout `holds_uncommitted` for as long as the worktree exists.
.claude/worktrees/
